# Harness loop & termination

Every agent run follows: `observe → think → act → evaluate → repeat | terminate | escalate`.
The harness owns context, tools, budgets, and termination — the model proposes, the harness
decides whether to continue.

Terminal states (use these exact names in code — enums, log fields, API responses):

| Condition | Outcome |
|---|---|
| Evaluator satisfied | `SUCCESS` |
| Budget exhausted (iterations/time/tokens/USD) | `PARTIAL` — best-so-far, flagged degraded |
| Same failure signature twice in a row | `FAILED_NO_PROGRESS` — stop immediately, do not retry a third time |
| Non-retryable error / human trigger | `FAILED` / `ESCALATED` |

For Video Agent specifically, the QC/repair loop is a bounded instance of this pattern:
repair attempts are capped at 2 per shot (see `.cursor/rules/15-video-pipeline.mdc`), and
cap exhaustion must resolve to `PARTIAL` (ship the best shot, flagged degraded) — never to
silently dropping the shot.
